1
00:00:00,450 --> 00:00:02,324
Air Carrier, CVN-79.

2
00:00:02,644 --> 00:00:07,485
Six MCP servers and a set of governed agents that give one aircraft carrier

3
00:00:07,485 --> 00:00:12,520
a cost the Navy can defend, and a pattern that carries to every major program.

4
00:00:12,840 --> 00:00:18,370
This is our entry in the GSA MCP Server and AI Agent Government Hackathon,

5
00:00:18,370 --> 00:00:20,985
in the Dataset Access Server track.

6
00:00:23,185 --> 00:00:24,262
Here is the problem.

7
00:00:24,582 --> 00:00:31,270
The USS John F. Kennedy, CVN-79, has four official cost figures, and none of them agree.

8
00:00:31,590 --> 00:00:40,020
The fiscal 2019 estimate is 11,341 million dollars. The statutory cap is 11,398 million.

9
00:00:40,020 --> 00:00:50,844
The Navy's cost limitation baseline is 12,936 million. The fiscal 2027 budget puts the ship at 13,409.97 million.

10
00:00:51,164 --> 00:00:57,051
Underneath sit 59 open questions, payments the public record cannot show,

11
00:00:57,051 --> 00:01:03,261
and a 13,529 million dollar figure printed in a report but not yet confirmed.

12
00:01:03,581 --> 00:01:05,945
Today analysts reconcile these by hand,

13
00:01:05,945 --> 00:01:10,006
for weeks, and a leader still has to pick one figure and defend it.

14
00:01:12,206 --> 00:01:15,349
We built one reusable architecture in six parts.

15
00:01:15,669 --> 00:01:21,166
MCP A Creator builds servers. The docs and ops servers read the budget books,

16
00:01:21,166 --> 00:01:25,593
oversight reports and contract records as exact, cited tables.

17
00:01:25,913 --> 00:01:29,731
The analyst server investigates records that are missing data.

18
00:01:29,731 --> 00:01:35,704
The One Hub server and its gate keep any figure out of a product until deterministic checks pass.

19
00:01:36,024 --> 00:01:38,922
The front center delivers all of it to people,

20
00:01:38,922 --> 00:01:45,223
with four specialist agents that propose and a person who decides. And a probe watches every server.

21
00:01:45,543 --> 00:01:50,357
Unity Catalog decides who may act, under the signed-in user's own identity.

22
00:01:52,557 --> 00:01:56,675
All of it runs on Databricks today. These are the seven apps:

23
00:01:56,675 --> 00:02:02,819
the ops, One Hub, docs and analyst servers, MCP A Creator, the probe, and the front center.

24
00:02:03,139 --> 00:02:07,309
Each one deploys from the public GitHub repository with one command,

25
00:02:07,309 --> 00:02:11,480
and the deploy checks that each app runs the commit that was pushed.

26
00:02:12,680 --> 00:02:15,613
Six MCP servers expose 63 tools.

27
00:02:15,933 --> 00:02:22,545
The docs server reads 34 PDFs, 7,804 pages, down to the page and table,

28
00:02:22,545 --> 00:02:29,995
with no model in the loop. On the deployed store, 7,743 of 7,746 tie-outs match.

29
00:02:30,315 --> 00:02:34,964
The analyst server works a record that is missing data and names what to ask for.

30
00:02:35,284 --> 00:02:37,836
The ops server serves exhibit cells,

31
00:02:37,836 --> 00:02:43,012
obligations, and the variance and work registers. MCP A Creator built it.

32
00:02:43,332 --> 00:02:47,253
The One Hub server holds the gate, the falsification checks,

33
00:02:47,253 --> 00:02:53,003
exact tie-outs and the gap queue. It is deployed, with an output schema on all 16 tools.

34
00:02:53,323 --> 00:02:56,107
The bakehouse server, also built by the Creator,

35
00:02:56,107 --> 00:02:59,240
reads a sales table that has nothing to do with ships.

36
00:02:59,560 --> 00:03:03,435
Every input is validated, and 421 hostile calls against

37
00:03:03,435 --> 00:03:07,450
the read tools wrote nothing and pasted nothing into SQL.

38
00:03:09,650 --> 00:03:12,157
MCP A Creator is the part that scales.

39
00:03:12,477 --> 00:03:16,563
Give it a question and a Unity Catalog table. It profiles the table,

40
00:03:16,563 --> 00:03:23,353
designs one tool per question, shows how it read the question so the owner can correct it, and reviews each tool.

41
00:03:23,673 --> 00:03:28,441
It generates a full project with tests, an evaluation kit and security lint,

42
00:03:28,441 --> 00:03:33,585
and deploys it as the requester's own app, with approval bound to the exact files.

43
00:03:33,905 --> 00:03:42,963
Fifteen of fifteen generated projects pass their own tests. One specification produces 58 of 58 byte-identical files.

44
00:03:42,963 --> 00:03:51,480
Release 1.0.0rc3 installs with uvx, and an upgrade regenerates a server without overwriting the owner's edits.

45
00:03:51,800 --> 00:03:54,418
An agency that holds its data in Unity

46
00:03:54,418 --> 00:03:58,206
Catalog gets a governed MCP server without a developer.

47
00:04:00,406 --> 00:04:05,271
The front center opens on The stack: seven capabilities, each useful on its own.

48
00:04:05,591 --> 00:04:09,659
For each one, the page shows the problem it solves, who else can use it,

49
00:04:09,659 --> 00:04:14,010
where it stands today, how it was tested, and what each result does not show.

50
00:04:14,330 --> 00:04:18,565
Security is laid out by risk, with the control that answers each risk.

51
00:04:19,765 --> 00:04:23,683
Impact answers the bigger question: one carrier read to the cent,

52
00:04:23,683 --> 00:04:27,059
and the same agents and servers for every weapon system.

53
00:04:27,379 --> 00:04:33,589
The flow is simple. You ask. Agents plan. MCP servers fetch. The gate checks. You decide.

54
00:04:33,909 --> 00:04:37,773
A new program gets its own governed server without a developer,

55
00:04:37,773 --> 00:04:40,778
because each program supplies data, not software.

56
00:04:41,098 --> 00:04:45,522
Four Ford class hulls are already loaded from the budget books.

57
00:04:45,522 --> 00:04:49,666
The F-35 uses the same method, with lots in place of hulls.

58
00:04:49,986 --> 00:04:54,638
At the bottom, each of the 59 programs with a fiscal 2027 Selected

59
00:04:54,638 --> 00:05:00,207
Acquisition Report is listed with what is loaded today and what it still needs.

60
00:05:01,407 --> 00:05:06,333
Inside the Department, moving to the next program is a set of inputs, not a rebuild.

61
00:05:06,653 --> 00:05:08,603
The Creator, the document reader,

62
00:05:08,603 --> 00:05:12,916
the investigation method, the gate and the agents are reused as they are.

63
00:05:13,236 --> 00:05:17,295
A program adds its documents, its contract numbers and program codes,

64
00:05:17,295 --> 00:05:22,825
and a subject total. The gate's floor is a share of that total, so it scales with the program.

65
00:05:23,145 --> 00:05:25,977
CVN-79 leads to the Ford class,

66
00:05:25,977 --> 00:05:32,462
then 29 Navy ship lines, the F-35, and all 59 programs on one template.

67
00:05:34,662 --> 00:05:38,883
Beyond defense, every agency has the same shape of problem:

68
00:05:38,883 --> 00:05:47,039
budget justifications, contract and grant records on USAspending and FPDS, and audit findings it cannot yet close.

69
00:05:47,359 --> 00:05:52,231
The servers, the gate and the agents carry over. What changes is the documents,

70
00:05:52,231 --> 00:05:57,288
the identifiers that isolate the subject, and the role map that names who decides.

71
00:05:57,608 --> 00:06:02,628
That covers major construction, grants, IT investments, and audit remediation.

72
00:06:04,828 --> 00:06:11,001
Back in the front center. The Brief asks what we can say about CVN-79's cost today.

73
00:06:11,321 --> 00:06:14,192
It runs in four steps: start from your question,

74
00:06:14,192 --> 00:06:18,677
check what you can say today, act on what is still open, and use the tools.

75
00:06:19,877 --> 00:06:21,759
The ship page holds the record:

76
00:06:21,759 --> 00:06:27,405
identity, key dates, and the program spine of every milestone, with construction photographs.

77
00:06:35,277 --> 00:06:40,391
Position answers the first question a leader asks: which figure do I quote, and for what?

78
00:06:40,711 --> 00:06:45,456
The short answer is four different kinds of number. The page shows where each sits,

79
00:06:45,456 --> 00:06:50,143
compares every pair, and walks the bridge from the cap to the budget step by step.

80
00:06:50,463 --> 00:06:54,016
It also names the difference that cannot yet be explained,

81
00:06:54,016 --> 00:06:56,896
and the record reconciliation ladder behind it.

82
00:06:58,096 --> 00:07:01,501
Here is the agentic workflow, live. From Position,

83
00:07:01,501 --> 00:07:06,948
a specialist run explains a File C period that does not tie to the transactions.

84
00:07:07,268 --> 00:07:10,293
The orchestrator routes it to the Account Analyst.

85
00:07:10,293 --> 00:07:13,197
The steps stream in, each labeled code or model.

86
00:07:13,517 --> 00:07:18,506
File C exceeds the closest transaction window by 770 million dollars.

87
00:07:18,506 --> 00:07:26,676
The run proposes a residual lead for the Office of Financial Operations, and a request for the obligation detail.

88
00:07:26,996 --> 00:07:33,063
Now the access control. The signed-in user holds the program office role, PMS 379.

89
00:07:33,063 --> 00:07:41,127
The first proposal belongs to Financial Operations, so the app says so and refuses to let this user apply it.

90
00:07:41,447 --> 00:07:46,279
The second proposal is owned by the program office. The user ticks it and applies it,

91
00:07:46,279 --> 00:07:49,690
and the action is recorded with the role and the run number.

92
00:07:50,890 --> 00:07:53,226
Every run follows the same six stages.

93
00:07:53,546 --> 00:07:59,241
A page triggers one task on one subject. The router refuses any pair it does not know.

94
00:07:59,241 --> 00:08:03,215
Code packs the records, with every figure in exact decimals.

95
00:08:03,535 --> 00:08:09,334
One model explains. It cannot add a figure, change an amount, or change who owns an item.

96
00:08:09,334 --> 00:08:14,676
Code then grounds every number, and a model from a second family reads the answer.

97
00:08:14,996 --> 00:08:20,620
Last, only the role that owns an item can apply it. Unity Catalog makes that call

98
00:08:20,620 --> 00:08:26,313
under the user's own token, against a dated role map. No role travels in the page.

99
00:08:26,633 --> 00:08:28,137
Four specialists run this way.

100
00:08:30,337 --> 00:08:33,513
This is the same decision on the deployed app today.

101
00:08:33,513 --> 00:08:37,850
The proposal owned by another office is locked, with the reason stated.

102
00:08:39,050 --> 00:08:46,843
Cost composition breaks the 13,409.97 million dollar total down by cost category and by funding stream,

103
00:08:46,843 --> 00:08:53,879
and shows what each named contract or vendor line accounts for, down to equipment line items.

104
00:08:55,079 --> 00:08:59,354
Cost growth shows the estimate in each successive budget submission,

105
00:08:59,354 --> 00:09:01,869
and the statutory cap history behind it.

106
00:09:03,069 --> 00:09:07,774
Budget execution shows the obligation curve and the handoff between contracts,

107
00:09:07,774 --> 00:09:12,840
the appropriation map from the contract's own account file, and the largest actions.

108
00:09:16,069 --> 00:09:20,944
The gap register asks which open questions block the number, and who can close them.

109
00:09:21,264 --> 00:09:24,718
It splits the work into what can be done now with no access,

110
00:09:24,718 --> 00:09:26,617
and what needs an access request.

111
00:09:26,937 --> 00:09:30,839
The discovery queue plots each gap by what is at stake and how

112
00:09:30,839 --> 00:09:35,182
easily it can be closed. And the last table names who can close what.

113
00:09:48,369 --> 00:09:54,379
From any gap, a run drafts the request. Here the Gap Investigator works gap G52.

114
00:09:54,699 --> 00:09:59,292
It proposes collection requests addressed to the offices that hold the records,

115
00:09:59,292 --> 00:10:01,734
and the checker re-checks every condition.

116
00:10:02,054 --> 00:10:05,350
Nothing is saved until a person with the right role applies it.

117
00:10:11,095 --> 00:10:15,815
The variance register records every place where sources disagree, and the reason.

118
00:10:19,495 --> 00:10:23,455
Asset valuation explains the three structural reasons the value

119
00:10:23,455 --> 00:10:26,597
on the Navy's books will never equal program cost.

120
00:10:27,797 --> 00:10:32,279
Who builds what shows the prime contractors and, at tier two, the sub-award map.

121
00:10:38,897 --> 00:10:43,170
Ask the evidence takes a plain question and answers it from the same records.

122
00:10:44,370 --> 00:10:49,934
What was obligated on the contract in fiscal 2022, and what was the largest action?

123
00:10:49,934 --> 00:10:55,096
The answer comes back as a lead, with its citation and the records behind it.

124
00:10:59,278 --> 00:11:02,359
On the deployed app, Ask is now an MCP host.

125
00:11:02,359 --> 00:11:08,173
It calls the docs, ops and One Hub servers, and each step names the server it used.

126
00:11:08,493 --> 00:11:14,923
Asked whether CVN-79 can be briefed at 13,529 million, it ties out the exhibit,

127
00:11:14,923 --> 00:11:21,760
runs four checks, and calls the result a verification lead, not a reportable figure.

128
00:11:22,960 --> 00:11:27,425
A second question: which File C periods fail to tie to the transactions,

129
00:11:27,425 --> 00:11:33,936
and by how much? The wait is cut. The answer lists each period and its difference, with the SQL that ran.

130
00:11:38,180 --> 00:11:41,808
The work queue shows what needs a decision, what is blocked, and why.

131
00:11:43,008 --> 00:11:47,312
Code sorts every item into one lane: decide, unblock, or system.

132
00:11:47,632 --> 00:11:49,375
Each run keeps its full record:

133
00:11:49,375 --> 00:11:52,973
the steps, the checks code ran again, and the checker's verdict.

134
00:11:56,964 --> 00:12:01,851
Brief readiness shows what is waiting on a decision, what the brief can stand on,

135
00:12:01,851 --> 00:12:07,341
obligations by contract, File C against the transactions, and the gaps that block the most.

136
00:12:08,541 --> 00:12:13,769
Live, 13 of 32 CVN-79 figures tie to source records.

137
00:12:14,089 --> 00:12:22,260
The Obligation Reconciler sums 927 actions on the detail design and construction contract in exact decimals,

138
00:12:22,260 --> 00:12:27,632
4,578,603,345.77 dollars, and code re-checks eight of eight conditions.

139
00:12:33,905 --> 00:12:38,302
The run log records every agent run and every action by every person.

140
00:12:39,502 --> 00:12:43,802
The detail table filters and exports the records behind every figure,

141
00:12:43,802 --> 00:12:46,607
and the exhibit table holds the budget cells.

142
00:12:47,807 --> 00:12:51,011
Sources lists the corpus and lets you search it:

143
00:12:51,011 --> 00:12:57,888
22 indexed documents, 9 structured sources kept as tables rather than embedded, and 12 sets of imagery.

144
00:13:02,507 --> 00:13:08,822
Method explains how this is built and why it can be challenged: three trust zones with a one-way door,

145
00:13:08,822 --> 00:13:15,695
what the method got wrong and kept on purpose, and the one rule everything follows. No model promotes a figure.

146
00:13:16,896 --> 00:13:22,095
Rules lists every rule code, the rulebook, the rule register, and the routes through the gate.

147
00:13:25,696 --> 00:13:28,162
The coverage map shows six layers of cost,

148
00:13:28,162 --> 00:13:32,389
where the other costs hide, and the asks in order of how cheap they are.

149
00:13:33,996 --> 00:13:37,751
Finally, the people who know. Answer a question opens the

150
00:13:37,751 --> 00:13:41,836
59 open questions to experts at headquarters and in the field.

151
00:13:42,156 --> 00:13:44,768
Each question names who is likely to know:

152
00:13:44,768 --> 00:13:50,739
the program office, financial operations, the supervisor of shipbuilding, or the finance center.

153
00:13:51,939 --> 00:13:53,660
An expert writes what they know,

154
00:13:53,660 --> 00:13:57,264
how they know it, and how sure they are, and can attach a document.

155
00:13:57,584 --> 00:14:00,516
The answer is recorded with their name as a lead,

156
00:14:00,516 --> 00:14:05,902
routed to the gap it answers, and never treated as a certified figure until it is checked.

157
00:14:10,892 --> 00:14:14,588
This turns what a few people know into evidence anyone can check.

158
00:14:14,908 --> 00:14:18,234
A field engineer who ran an interface for four years,

159
00:14:18,234 --> 00:14:24,508
or a headquarters analyst who knows which ledger holds an account, can close a gap in two sentences.

160
00:14:24,828 --> 00:14:28,049
The gap register shows which office owns each question,

161
00:14:28,049 --> 00:14:32,147
the work queue routes the answer, and the run log keeps who said what.

162
00:14:34,347 --> 00:14:44,758
On 69 sealed questions, hashed before any model saw them, Claude Sonnet 4.5 answers 88.4 percent with the servers,

163
00:14:44,758 --> 00:14:51,242
against 14.5 percent without. GPT-5 mini goes from 1.4 to 78.7 percent.

164
00:14:51,562 --> 00:14:58,482
On questions written by an evaluator outside the team, Claude scores 25 of 30,

165
00:14:58,482 --> 00:15:05,223
83.3 percent, and GPT-5 mini 63.3 percent. Without tools, each gets 1 of 10.

166
00:15:05,543 --> 00:15:08,863
A separate external reviewer, blind to the source,

167
00:15:08,863 --> 00:15:13,377
would rely on 9 of 10 answers with the servers, and 0 of 10 without.

168
00:15:13,697 --> 00:15:20,516
1,762 tests pass from a clean clone, 828 of them hostile inputs.

169
00:15:20,516 --> 00:15:29,891
The probe passes 99.90 percent of 6,193 checks, with 1,234 of 1,234 known answers right.

170
00:15:32,091 --> 00:15:33,107
It is built to run.

171
00:15:33,427 --> 00:15:38,242
Every app requires workspace sign-in and runs as its own service principal.

172
00:15:38,242 --> 00:15:40,873
Decisions run under the user's own token.

173
00:15:41,193 --> 00:15:45,783
Tool inputs are validated and capped, identifiers are allow-listed,

174
00:15:45,783 --> 00:15:51,810
and parameters are bound. pip-audit and bandit run in CI and in every generated project.

175
00:15:52,130 --> 00:15:58,081
The probe calls every deployed server every 15 minutes, and alerts when a known answer changes.

176
00:16:00,281 --> 00:16:03,435
One ship, measured to the cent, and ready for the next program.

177
00:16:03,755 --> 00:16:08,332
The code, the scorecard, the evaluation and the findings are in the repository,

178
00:16:08,332 --> 00:16:11,633
and every page can be clicked through without an account.
